    {
      "id": "70432270-4675-4a05-8048-86a57c737740",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        368,
        4896
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 880,
        "height": 736,
        "content": "## ✅ Meeting Notes to Action Items – ClickUp, Notion & Slack\n\n### How it works\nTwo triggers feed the same pipeline. **Telegram:** paste or forward meeting notes as a text message to your bot. **Google Drive:** drop a `.txt` transcript into a monitored folder. Both normalise the transcript, validate its length (min 20 words — short messages are skipped), then detect meeting type from keywords (Planning, Retrospective, Standup, Review). After a 1s rate-limit Wait, GPT-4o-mini extracts a summary and action items (owner, due date, priority). Each action item becomes a ClickUp task. If tasks were created, a Slack summary posts to the team channel. A Notion page is created with the full meeting metadata. Everything is logged to Airtable for your records. A Telegram confirmation closes the loop.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Telegram Bot API** to `Telegram Trigger` and `Send Telegram Confirmation`.\n2. Connect **Google Drive OAuth2** to `Google Drive Trigger` + `Download Transcript File`.\n3. Connect **OpenAI API** to `AI Extract Action Items`.\n4. Connect **ClickUp API** → replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CLICKUP_LIST_ID`.\n5. Connect **Slack OAuth2** → replace `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID` in both Slack nodes.\n6. Connect **Notion API** → replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_NOTION_MEETING_NOTES_DATABASE_ID`.\n7. Connect **Airtable PAT** → replace base and table IDs.\n8. Activate both triggers."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "95f2c49d-a0de-4273-8b1b-9621d413c7e9",
      "name": "Section – Dual Transcript Intake1",
